// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/numeric/paper_claims.t27 -- which numbers printed in three papers about our formats can be recomputed,
; and which of them come out the same. Every recomputation is exact integer arithmetic in this file.
; --
; The papers:
;   P_GF    arXiv:2606.05017v5, GoldenFloat: e = round((N-1)/phi^2), f = N-1-e.
;   P_RULER arXiv:2606.09686v3, the Golden Ruler catalog: 109 formats, 12 clusters, six conformance packs.
;   P_TNF   "TNF" by Dmitrii Vasilev (2026-08-11): four families GF, GF-T, BNF, TNF; 1 + Et + M = N.
;   P_REPO  the format specs of this repository (specs/numeric/gft*.t27, tnf*.t27, bnf*.t27).
; --
; The rules:
; - A claim row holds what the paper prints (CL_PRINTED, in the unit CL_UNIT with CL_DEC decimals) and a
;   recomputation (CL_KIND, CL_ARG). verdict_of() is V_FITS when the recomputed value equals the printed
;   one exactly, V_MISFIT when it does not, and V_UNCHECKED when no recomputation exists (CL_KIND = K_NONE):
;   a testbench run, a cross-validation against another library, a measured magnitude count.
; - Count rows (U_COUNT) print how many entries of a table the paper claims and recompute how many hold.
; - Irrational constants are never written down. sqrt(5) enters only through isqrt(5 a^2); ln 2, ln 3 and e
;   are summed as series at scale 10^12; a rounded decimal is compared as an integer.
; - Rounding to three significant digits is half-to-even at an exact tie: 2^-5 = 3.125e-2 prints 3.12e-2.
; - The repo widths below (GFT_*, TNF_*, BNF_*) are a snapshot of specs/numeric at eb425e6ac, taken so the
;   paper tables can be compared with them; the format specs stay the source of those widths.
; - The catalog counts CATALOG_RECORDS and CATALOG_CLUSTERS are measured on specs/numeric/formats_catalog.t27
;   (`t27c catalog-gate` reports 109 records; its cluster= fields name 13 distinct clusters).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module NumericPaperClaims;

